id: pm-beads-uwkq
title: Queue trailing separated heredoc after joined opener
description: "Fix Greptile PR 88 finding 3890010994: a mixed cat <<A<< B opener queues only A, exposing B body assignments."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-30T17:17:12.722Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-30T17:22:31.506Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-30T17:22:10.483Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-30T17:22:10.483Z"
author: pi-agent
severity: high
repro_steps: Review thread 3890010994; cat <<A<< B followed by a provenance-shaped assignment in body B.
resolution: Queue both joined and trailing separated heredoc delimiters from the same shell token.
expected_result: Every heredoc body opened by a mixed joined/separated command remains excluded from shell scalar state.
actual_result: The trailing separated delimiter is dropped when an earlier joined delimiter matched.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T17:22:09.384Z",pi-agent,"Greptile finding 3890010994 reproduced: focused regression failed with actual --provenance when only scripts/shell-command-scan.ts was reverted, SOURCE_ONLY_REVERT_EXIT=1. The fix independently queues a trailing separated heredoc after joined matches. Restored source passed the focused test. pm linked tests passed npm test, coverage, docstring, and release:check with zero assertion, timeout, or infrastructure failures."
